ion operations allocates managed memory.","Recommendation":"Try to avoid concatenating strings in frequently-updated code. Prefer using a StringBuilder instead, as this minimizes managed allocations.","DocumentationUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.concat","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1003","Title":"System.DateTime.Now","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.DateTime.Now</b> can take a lot of CPU time because it needs to figure out the current timezone and daylight saving time information.","Recommendation":"Try to avoid using this method in frequently-updated code. Prefer UnityEngine.Time.time or, if precise time is needed, use DateTime.UtcNow.","DocumentationUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.datetime.now","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1004","Title":"System.AppDomain.GetAssemblies","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.AppDomain.GetAssemblies</b> can take a lot of CPU time.","Recommendation":"Try to minimize calls to <b>System.AppDomain.GetAssemblies</b> by caching the returned assemblies. When possible, use <b>UnityEditor.TypeCache</b> for fast access to types, methods and fields.","DocumentationUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.appdomain.getassemblies","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0232","Title":"UnityEditor.AssetDatabase.FindAssets","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>UnityEditor.AssetDatabase.FindAssets</b> is a CPU-intensive operation and can slow down the Editor for long periods of time on large projects.","Recommendation":"Try to minimize calls to <b>UnityEditor.AssetDatabase.FindAssets</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/AssetDatabase.FindAssets.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0234","Title":"UnityEngine.Object.FindObjectOfType","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Object.FindObjectOfType()</b> allocates managed memory and can be slow.","Recommendation":"Try to avoid calling this method in frequently-updated code. Ideally, this method should only be used during initialisation, and the results should be cached if they need to be re-used.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Object.FindObjectOfType.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0192","Title":"Debug.Log / Debug.LogFormat","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Debug.Log</b> methods take a lot of CPU time, especially if used frequently.","Recommendation":"Remove logging code, or strip it from release builds by using scripting symbols for conditional compilation (#if ... #endif) or the <b>ConditionalAttribute</b> on a custom logging method that calls Debug.Log. Where logging is required in release builds, CPU times can be reduced by disabling stack traces in log messages. You can do this by setting <b>Application.SetStackTraceLogType(LogType.Log, StackTraceLogType.None)</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UnderstandingPerformanceGeneralOptimizations.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0193","Title":"Debug.LogWarning / Debug.LogWarningFormat","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Debug.LogWarning</b> methods take a lot of CPU time, especially if used frequently.","Recommendation":"Remove logging code, or strip it from release builds by using scripting symbols for conditional compilation (#if ... #endif) or the <b>ConditionalAttribute</b> on a custom logging method that calls Debug.LogWarning. Where logging is required in release builds, CPU times can be reduced by disabling stack traces in log messages. You can do this by setting <b>Application.SetStackTraceLogType(LogType.Log, StackTraceLogType.None)</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UnderstandingPerformanceGeneralOptimizations.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4000","Title":"Audio: Long AudioClip is not set to Streaming","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip has a runtime memory footprint larger than the streaming buffer size of 200KB, but its <b>Load Type</b> is not set to <b>Streaming</b>. Storing the whole clip in memory rather than streaming it may be an inefficient use of memory.","Recommendation":"Consider setting <b>Load Type</b> to <b>Streaming</b> in the AudioClip Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4001","Title":"Audio: Short AudioClip is set to streaming","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip has a runtime memory footprint smaller than the streaming buffer size of 200KB, but its <b>Load Type</b> is set to <b>Streaming</b>. Requiring a streaming buffer for this clip is an inefficient use of memory.","Recommendation":"Set <b>Load Type</b> to <b>Compressed in Memory</b> or <b>Decompress On Load</b> in the AudioClip Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4003","Title":"Audio: AudioClip is stereo","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory, Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The audio source asset is in stereo, <b>Force To Mono</b> is not enabled in the AudioClip Import Settings, and the <b>Load Type</b> is not <b>Streaming</b>, which implies the AudioClip may be used as a diagetic positional sound effect. Positional effects should be mono; only non-diagetic music and effects should be stereo.","Recommendation":"Tick the <b>Force To Mono</b> checkbox in the AudioClip Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4004","Title":"Audio: AudioClip is set to Decompress On Load","Areas":{"m_String":"LoadTime, Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip is long, and its <b>Load Type</b> is set to <b>Decompress On Load</b>. The clip's memory footprint may be excessive, and decompression may impact load times.","Recommendation":"Consider setting the <b>Load Type</b> to <b>Compressed In Memory</b> or <b>Streaming</b>. If you have concerns about the CPU cost of decompressing <b>Compressed In Memory</b> clips for playback, consider a format which is fast to decompress, such as <b>ADPCM</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4005","Title":"Audio: Compressed AudioClip is Compressed In Memory","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip's <b>Load Type</b> is set to <b>Compressed In Memory</b> but the clip is imported with a format that is not trivial to decompress. Decompression will be performed every time the clip is played, and may impact CPU performance.","Recommendation":"If runtime performance is impacted, either set the <b>Load Type</b> to <b>Decompress On Load</b> or set the <b>Compression Format</b> to <b>ADPCM</b>, which is fast to decompress.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4007","Title":"Audio: Sample Rate is over 48 kHz","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize, LoadTime, Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip's source sample rate is higher than 48 kHz, and the <b>Sample Rate Setting</b> does not override it. Most Blu-Rays are at 48kHz, and higher sample rates are generally only used during the recording process or for scientific data. If compression is applied during the import process the sample rate gets capped at 48kHz. If compression isn't applied, the runtime memory footprint for this clip will be excessive. In both cases, the source file size is excessive.","Recommendation":"Set the <b>Sample Rate Setting</b> to <b>Override</b> and the <b>Sample Rate</b> to <b>48000</b> Hz or lower.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4008","Title":"Audio: Preload Audio Data is enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"LoadTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Preload Audio Data</b> checkbox is ticked for this AudioClip. This forces scene/prefab loading to wait synchronously until the AudioClip has completed loading before continuing running, and can impact scene load/initialization times.","Recommendation":"Consider un-ticking the <b>Preload Audio Data</b> checkbox. Audio preloading is only required when the AudioClip must play at the exact moment the scene begins simulating, or if the audio timing must be very precise the first time it is played.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4009","Title":"Audio: Load In Background is not enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, LoadTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"This AudioClip is large, and the <b>Load In Background</b> checkbox is not ticked. Loading will be performed synchronously and will block the main thread. This may impact load times or create CPU spikes, depending on when the clip is loaded.","Recommendation":"Tick the <b>Load In Background</b> checkbox in the AudioClip Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4010","Title":"Audio: Compression Format is MP3","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip's <b>Compression Format</b> is set to <b>MP3</b>. MP3 is an old compression format which has been surpassed in efficiency and quality by newer formats such as Vorbis.","Recommendation":"Set the <b>Compression Format</b> to <b>Vorbis</b> in the AudioClip's Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4011","Title":"Audio: Source asset is in a lossy compressed format","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The file format used by the source asset for the AudioClip uses a lossy compression format. The Asset Import process decompresses the audio data and recompresses it in the chosen runtime format. This may result in a further loss of sound quality.","Recommendation":"Wherever possible, select a lossless file format such as .WAV or .AIFF for source assets.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA1000","Title":"Mesh: Read/Write enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> flag in the Model Import Settings is enabled. This causes the mesh data to be duplicated in memory.","Recommendation":"If not required, disable the <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> option in the Model Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/FBXImporter-Model.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA1001","Title":"Mesh: Index Format is 32 bits","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Index Format</b> in the Model Import Settings is set to <b>32 bit</b>, but the model does not have enough vertices to require 32 bit indices. This increases the mesh size and may not work on certain mobile devices.","Recommendation":"Consider using changing the <b>Index Format</b> option in the Model Import Settings. This should be set to either <b>16 bits</b> or <b>Auto</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/FBXImporter-Model.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA1002","Title":"Mesh: Read/Write enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> flag is enabled. This causes the mesh data to be duplicated in memory.","Recommendation":"If not required, disable the <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> option via script or by using the Quick Fix button.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Mesh-isReadable.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA1003","Title":"Mesh: Index Format is 32 bits","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The mesh's <b>Index Format</b> is <b>32 bit</b>, but the mesh does not have enough vertices to require 32 bit indices. This increases the mesh size and may not work on certain mobile devices.","Recommendation":"Rebuild the mesh with a <b>16 bit</b> Index Format, either via script or by using the Quick Fix button.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Mesh-indexFormat.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA3000","Title":"Resources folder asset","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Resources folder</b> is a common source of many problems in Unity projects. Improper use of the Resources folder can bloat the size of a project's build, lead to uncontrollable excessive me